 # Domain Memory — pi-workflows
 
 ## Glossary
+- **subway map**: the conversation-tree visualization — vertical node/edge strip (turns, forks, edits, gates, pending) rendered beside/over the transcript; nodes clickable, details scroll in the main pane.
+- **settle-judge**: the async formatting pattern — deterministic heuristics first; a cheap typed call (`models.classify()`/flash-class) only on uncertain nodes, fired on turn settle; placeholder-then-patch so display never blocks; cache by (entryId, textHash, rubricVersion).
 - **abort-as-failure-signal**: when a needs-gated reviewer node auto-aborts (upstream worker failed/blocked), no verdict exists; the orchestrator treats the abort itself as the failure signal and inspects the worker output directly.
 - **verification policy**: registry table mapping task traits (docs / standard / security-concurrency-parsing-external-input) to reviewer model+thinking; scales reviewer cost, never its existence.
 
